---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Docs title="Quickstart">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-10 prose">
    <h1>Quickstart</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Your first agent task in five steps.</p>

    <h2>1. Launch Craig</h2>
    <pre><code>craig</code></pre>
    <p>The boot overlay plays, then Craig's workspace opens.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 my-6"><div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-[#292e42]">
    <img src="/screenshots/launch.png" alt="Craig TUI on first launch" class="w-full block" /></div>
  </div>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-10 prose">
    <h2>2. Add a repo (first time only)</h2>
    <p>Select <strong>+ New Workspace</strong> from the left panel, or run:</p>
    <pre><code>craig workspace add /path/to/your/repo</code></pre>

    <h2>3. Create a task</h2>
    <p>
      Press <kbd>n</kbd> from the TUI, type a short task description, and press <kbd>Enter</kbd>.
      Craig creates a task record, branch, git worktree, and agent tab.
    </p>
    <p>
      The task text is used as Craig task metadata. It is not pasted into the agent automatically;
      once the agent PTY opens, give the runner the instructions you want it to follow.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Watch the agent work</h2>
    <p>
      Press <kbd>Enter</kbd> on the agent tab to attach its live PTY.
      Press <kbd>Ctrl+]</kbd> to return to Craig control mode.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 my-6"><div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-[#292e42]">
    <img src="/screenshots/agent-working.png" alt="Agent working in Craig TUI" class="w-full block" /></div>
  </div>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-10 prose">
    <h2>5. Review the work</h2>
    <p>
      Use the <strong>Changes</strong> and <strong>Review</strong> inspector panels to check the diff,
      inspect PR status, and refresh tracked check state. The Review panel is a read-only status surface;
      ask the agent in its PTY to run checks, commit, open PRs, or merge when that work is ready.
    </p>
    <p>
      The command layer exposes lower-level task operations such as
      <code>craig task check &lt;task-id&gt;</code> and <code>craig task commit &lt;task-id&gt;</code>
      for automation or agent-driven workflows.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 my-6"><div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-[#292e42]">
    <img src="/screenshots/ci-review.png" alt="CI checks passing in review panel" class="w-full block" /></div>
  </div>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-10 prose">
    <p>Next: <a href="/docs/tui">TUI Reference →</a></p>
  </div>
</Docs>
